# Blossoming Tortoise: when it enters it mills exactly three cards (the fourth, a Forest, stays on top of the library), then the
# controller returns a land card of their choice from the graveyard to the battlefield tapped (CR 701.17, 608.2c). The land is
# read after the mill, so a milled Mutavault is eligible; the milled Plains is left behind, and the milled Ornithopter, not a land
# card, is refused. Black Lotus (GGG) and Mox Jet pay {2}{G}{G}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Blossoming Tortoise
Island x4
Mutavault
Plains
Ornithopter
Forest
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Blossoming Tortoise.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Library.Count = 14
! Bot1.Choose()
! Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Choose(Forest)
Bot1.Choose(Mutavault)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Plains; Black Lotus
Bot1.Library.Count = 14
